# docs/ is deliberately NOT ignored: openapi.yaml is the API contract that
# `npm run check:api` verifies on every push, and the README links the ADRs
# and the runbook. Ignoring it meant CI checked a file the repository could
# never contain.
kodeBranding/

# Secrets and local config — never committed. INV-08.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Runtime data. The uploads directory holds member documents.
#
# Unanchored on purpose. These were written as `/data/` and
# `/apps/server/uploads/`, which are repo-root paths that nothing ever writes
# to: UPLOAD_DIR and SCAN_DIR default to `./data/uploads` and `./data/scans`
# *relative to the workspace the process runs in*, so `npm run dev -w
# @kode/server` puts them in `apps/server/data/`. Neither rule matched, and
# eighteen scanned member documents were committed before anyone noticed.
#
# `**/` on purpose, and it is the part that is easy to get wrong twice. A
# pattern containing a slash anywhere but the end — `data/uploads/` — is
# *already* anchored to the directory holding the .gitignore, so it matches only
# `<root>/data/uploads/`. Only a leading `**/` makes it match at any depth.
**/data/uploads/
**/data/scans/
**/data/spool/
**/logs/

